## Plus repos row→domain read mapping (snake_case bug) — branch `fix/pentest-script-rdd`, no commits
- [x] Defect confirmed: all three Plus repos read `SELECT *` and passed the row to `<Entity>.fromPlainObject({ ...row, <few overrides> })`; snake_case keys survived, camelCase fields arrived `undefined` → `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'includes')` at `plus/domain/entities/entitlement.ts:117/:140`. None of the three ever worked against a real DB.
- [x] NEW `plus/infrastructure/repositories/row-mappers.ts` — `mapEntitlementRow` / `mapPlusUserRow` / `mapResourceRow` + exported `EntitlementRow` / `PlusUserRow` / `ResourceRow` types. Every column renamed explicitly; `TEXT[]` NULL → `[]`; nullable optionals → `undefined`; `TIMESTAMPTZ` → ISO string (what `fromPlainObject`'s signature declares); `metadata` via `parseJsonbColumn` (jsonb.ts reused, no `JSON.parse(row.metadata)`). Style mirrors `PostgresChallengeRepository`'s `ChallengeRow`/`toChallengeProps`.
- [x] Replaced all **23** `fromPlainObject({ ...row, … })` call sites: 8 in `PostgresEntitlementRepository`, 7 in `PostgresPlusUserRepository`, 8 in `PostgresResourceRepository`. 0 `...row` spreads remain in `plus/`.
- [x] Write paths untouched (diff-verified): INSERT parameter arrays still read `plain.userId` / `plain.pestilloState` / `plain.habitualCountries` etc.
- [x] `PostgresEntitlementRepository.findByUserAndResource`: documented (comment only) that `` `${userId}:${resourceId}` `` IS the row key — intended convention, unchanged.
- [x] NEW `tests/plus/row-mappers.test.ts` — 14 tests, no DB: exact key-set per entity, pg-shaped fixtures (`Date` for timestamptz, JS array for `TEXT[]`, parsed object for jsonb), regression proving `allowedOperations` is an array and `.includes()` does not throw, proof the old `{...row}` spread throws the observed `TypeError`, NULL `TEXT[]` → `[]`, NULL optionals → `undefined`, NULL `active` → `false` (fail-closed; column is `BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE` with no `NOT NULL`).
- [x] Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit 2>&1 | grep -c '^plus/'` = **803** (exact baseline; 803/803 in `plus/admin`, `plus/api` 0, `plus/infrastructure` 0, `src/` 0); `npx jest --silent` = **1022 passed, 0 failed** (baseline 1008 + 14 new, 17 skipped unchanged).

REPORT — found, deliberately NOT fixed (outside this defect's scope):
- [ ] **Core `src/infrastructure/repositories/PostgresVaultRepository.ts` — same snake_case class, 6/6 read sites**: `SELECT … encrypted_data, encryption_key_id …` but `Vault.fromPlainObject` expects `encryptedData` / `encryptionKeyId`; neither is in the override list (`ownerId/metadata/createdAt/updatedAt/lockVersion` only) → both `undefined` on every Postgres vault read. `docs/correcciones.md` claims this was fixed; the date/owner fields were, these two were not.
- [ ] **Core `src/infrastructure/repositories/PostgresCredentialRepository.ts` — 6/6 read sites**: `release_share_ref` is selected but never mapped to `releaseShareRef` (optional in `Credential.fromPlainObject`) → lost on every read, i.e. H3's server-minted secret ref does not round-trip through Postgres.
- [ ] **Core `PostgresVaultRepository` / `PostgresCredentialRepository` — 6 sites**: `row.metadata ? JSON.parse(row.metadata) : undefined` on `metadata JSONB DEFAULT '{}'` — the identical `pg` jsonb double-parse that `plus/infrastructure/repositories/jsonb.ts` fixed for Plus; throws `SyntaxError: "[object Object]" is not valid JSON` on any non-NULL metadata.
- [ ] `plus_users.active` / `plus_resources.active` are `BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE` with no `NOT NULL` → NULL reachable; mapper maps it to `false` (fail-closed, matches the old spread's falsy runtime value). No DDL change made.
- [ ] `created_at` / `updated_at` are nullable-with-default in all three Plus tables; mappers type them as `Date` (same as `ChallengeRow`). A hand-inserted NULL yields the same `new Date(null)` → epoch it produced before; unchanged behaviour, not hardened.
- [ ] `PostgresChallengeRepository.toChallengeProps` hardcodes `assuranceLevel: 3` instead of reading `row.assurance_level` — checked, NOT a defect: `ChallengeProps.assuranceLevel` is the literal type `3` and every write binds `challenge.assuranceLevel`.

